Package: jaxR
Title: Composable Transformations of Array Programs in Native R
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Adam R", "Sophie", email = "adamrsophie@gmail.com",
                  role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: An R mirror of the 'JAX' Python package: composable function
    transformations (automatic differentiation in forward and reverse mode,
    vectorization with 'vmap', staging to 'jaxpr' and just in time compilation
    with 'jit'), a 'NumPy' compatible array interface, 'lax' primitives with
    structured control flow, counter based random numbers that match 'JAX' bit
    for bit, and 'SciPy' style special functions. Programs are lowered to
    'StableHLO' and compiled and executed by 'XLA' through the 'PJRT' C API;
    the runtime plugin is installed with install_pjrt().
License: GPL (>= 3)
URL: https://adamrsophie.github.io/jaxR/, https://github.com/adamrsophie/jaxR
BugReports: https://github.com/adamrsophie/jaxR/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.3.0)
